---
import { localeFromPath } from '@portfolio/i18n';
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import StripeCalculator from '../../components/calculators/StripeCalculator';
---
<ToolLayout title="Stripe fee calculator" description="See exactly what you keep—or what to charge. Calculate Stripe fees in MXN and USD with editable rates and Radar protection." category="Payments" image="stripe" checked="Rates checked September 26, 2026" app>
  <StripeCalculator locale={localeFromPath(Astro.url.pathname)} client:load />
  <div slot="guide" class="flex flex-col gap-8">
    <div class="prose-copy"><h2>A clearer view of every payment.</h2><p>Choose a Mexico / MXN or United States / USD account preset, enter a payment, and see processing costs, Radar, fee tax, and your remaining amount. To work backwards, select “I want to receive” and enter the amount you need to keep.</p></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>How are fees calculated?</summary><div class="prose-copy"><p>Processing fee = payment × (base rate + enabled surcharges) + fixed fee. Radar and any additional costs are added, then the selected tax is applied to those fees. Each component is rounded to cents.</p><p>The reverse calculator finds a charge in whole cents that leaves at least your desired amount after these rounded fees. Tiny differences from an actual invoice are possible.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Which Radar plan should I enter?</summary><div class="prose-copy"><p>Lite, Standard, Plus, and Pro presets populate pay-as-you-go per-screened-transaction costs. You can overwrite the Radar value for negotiated rates or your own estimate. Pro abuse events are separate; include any expected per-payment allocation in “Other per-payment costs.”</p><p>This estimates one successfully processed, screened payment. Radar can bill for screened payments that are later blocked, so a monthly invoice may differ. Subscriptions, platform account fees, disputes, refunds, and installment charges are excluded.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Where do the presets come from?</summary><div class="prose-copy"><p>Checked September 26, 2026 against <a href="https://stripe.com/mx/pricing">Stripe Mexico pricing</a>, <a href="https://stripe.com/pricing">Stripe US pricing</a>, and <a href="https://stripe.com/mx/radar/pricing">Radar pricing</a>. Mexican published processing prices exclude IVA; the editable 16% fee-tax assumption is included by default. Confirm the treatment on your account.</p><p>Currency is paired with an account-country preset. A Mexican account charging USD does not automatically qualify for US pricing. This independent tool is not affiliated with Stripe.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</ToolLayout>
